{"id": "EUVD-2026-102473", "enisaUuid": "9b5903d4-6c7a-338f-b48f-d9bc85b30253", "description": "Driftregion iso14229 before 0.10.1 contains an integer wraparound in Handle_0x38_RequestFileTransfer that lets unauthenticated attackers bypass the file path length check. Attackers can send a short RequestFileTransfer (SID 0x38) request with filePathAndNameLength 0xFFFC-0xFFFF, causing callbacks to read past the receive buffer, crashing targets or disclosing memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:57:41", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/driftregion/iso14229/security/advisories/GHSA-5hgv-5fqg-8vcr", "https://github.com/driftregion/iso14229/security/advisories/GHSA-ph4f-7v39-8hgm", "https://github.com/driftregion/iso14229/commit/2e36afcd7f0cd02b0c70446c1a265a7b1999d478", "https://github.com/driftregion/iso14229/blob/0.10.0/src/server.c#L1151-L1161", "https://github.com/driftregion/iso14229/releases/tag/0.10.1%2B9e7c47e8", "https://github.com/driftregion/iso14229", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/iso14229-before-0.10.1-out-of-bounds-read-via-handle-0x38-requestfiletransfer"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111282", "GHSA-w2jf-rrfp-47w9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7f4a3272-35aa-339a-b4e0-c97c3cb98dd4", "product": {"name": "iso14229", "vendor": {"name": "driftregion"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.10.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4cbafd11-beeb-34e9-a4b0-99d6ab27d54f", "vendor": {"name": "driftregion"}}], "isExploited": false}